    "VISUAL_NAME": "Card",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_WARRANTY_AMC_EXPIRING_30D",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "Management Dashboard tile VIS_004 — Warranty/AMC Expiring in 30 Days (Card). Counts assets whose Warranty coverage (FAM_WARRANTY_DETAILS.WARRANTY_END_DATE) or Active AMC contract coverage (FAM_AMC_CONTRACTS.STATUS='ACTIVE', END_DATE, via FAM_AMC_CONTRACT_LINE) falls within the next 30 days from today (CURRENT_DATE to CURRENT_DATE+30), matching the FRS trigger threshold for the Warranty/AMC renewal notification. ASSUMPTIONS: (1) Neither Warranty nor AMC tables carry a BRANCH_CODE column, so branch scope is resolved via a LEFT JOIN LATERAL to each asset's latest APPROVED FAM_ASSET_TRANSFER row (same proxy pattern used on sibling VIS_001/VIS_002/VIS_003 cards) — an asset never transferred has no branch match and is excluded when a specific branch is selected (default is 'All' via '%'). (2) Deliberately NOT scoped by FINANCIAL_YEAR — like VIS_003, this is a live rolling-window alert count (next 30 days from today), not a period trend; FY-scoping would be semantically wrong for an expiry countdown. (3) AMC count is COUNT(DISTINCT asset_code) across contract lines (an asset covered by one active soon-expiring contract counts once); Warranty count is COUNT(*) of warranty records in range (one warranty record per asset per the FRS 'Manage Warranty Details' one-active-record design). (4) The FRS's drill-through to the 'Warranty / AMC Expiry' Grid visual is configured at the DASHBOARD tile level (VISUAL_CONFIG_REF + drill binding), not inside this Visual object — out of scope for this file.",
    "SCHEMA_TYPE": "S",
    "OUTPUT_TYPE": "JSON",
    "DATABASE_TYPE": "1",
